1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,760
I remember walking out of the office and looking through a little clearing over on the next block,

2
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:13,440
which was right in front of the Monroe Street address and seeing a lot of police cars over there.

3
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:20,960
And at that time, Bible Russ came to the office, so he had just come from over there,

4
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:26,560
or maybe the coroner's office. In any case, we walked back over there and we both were

5
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:32,960
speechless. We just walked through the house and saw where what had taken place and where he died,

6
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:40,640
and it was shocking. And then I was, you know, I just began to realize that the information

7
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:52,160
that I supplied leading up to that moment had facilitated that raid. I knew that indirectly,

8
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:57,040
I had contributed, and I felt it, and I felt bad about it. And then I got mad.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,840
And then I had to conceal those feelings, which made it worse. I couldn't,

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,240
I couldn't say anything. I just had to continue to play the role.

11
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:16,720
FBI headquarters authorized payment of a $300 bonus to informant William O'Neill for quote,

12
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:24,560
uniquely valuable services which he rendered over the past several months. Unquote.

